Package: secubox-spiderfoot
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, secubox-core (>= 1.0.0), debootstrap, lxc, jq
Description: SpiderFoot OSINT automation engine (LXC-sandboxed)
 Runs the SpiderFoot OSINT automation engine inside a dedicated
 debootstrap/LXC sandbox — 200+ passive modules and a correlation graph,
 the interim Maltego-style correlation hub. SpiderFoot ships its own web
 UI and REST API bound to the container's LAN IP; this module handles the
 LXC lifecycle, a status probe, and reverse-proxies the container UI behind
 the SecuBox WAF/auth front. Features include:
  - 200+ passive OSINT modules with a correlation graph
  - Sandboxed execution in a dedicated LXC container
  - SpiderFoot's own UI/REST reachable ONLY via the WAF-fronted proxy
  - JWT-gated lifecycle API with append-only audit logging
  - Detached install/lifecycle model (never blocks the aggregator loop)
